  "prefLabel": "Nur 102.01 Composition and Functions",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Nur 102.01 Composition and Functions.\n\n(a) The board of nursing shall consist of 13 members appointed by the governor and council, pursuant to RSA 326-B:3.\n\n(b) The board shall adopt rules relative to:\n\n(1) Standards for nursing practice;\n\n(2) Criteria for nursing education programs;\n\n(3) Criteria for initial licensure, license renewal, and the reinstatement of licenses for registered and practical nurses, advanced registered nurse practitioners, and nursing assistants;\n\n(4) Criteria for certifying licensed nursing assistants to administer medication;\n\n(5) Ethical and professional standards for the practice of licensees;\n\n(6) The determination and enforcement of disciplinary action against all individuals found in violation of RSA 326-B or the rules adopted by the board;\n\n(7) The implementation of the nurse licensure compact set forth in RSA 326-B:46; and\n\n(8) Any other matters necessary for the proper administration of RSA 326-B.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note #1 at chapter heading for Nur 100) #5887, eff 8-26-94; ss by #6778, eff 6-26-98; ss by #7736, eff 8-6-02; ss by #8777, eff 12-23-06; ss by #10296, eff 3-22-13; ss by #10569, eff 4-17-14; ss by #14294, eff 6-27-25",
